n conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn7le11ob04re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Silent Letters in English ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You don't say every letter in a word in English pronunciation. Some letters are silent, which means that you don't hear them as you would pronounce them normally.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Here are examples of the silent letter <span class=\"italic\">b</span> in words. Practice saying the example sentences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Letter\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Words\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Pronunciation\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Examples\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Silent B\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" climb<br/><br/>   comb<br/><br/>  dumb<br/><br/>    doubt<br/><br/>  limbs<br/><br/>  numb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"clime <br/><br/>  cohme<br/><br/>  dum<br/><br/> dowt <br/><br/>  lim<br/><br/>  num\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I had to <span class=\\\"strong\\\">climb</span> the stairs.<br/><br/> I didn't have time to <span class=\\\"strong\\\">comb</span> my hair.<br/><br/> I kept saying <span class=\\\"strong\\\">dumb</span> things.<br/><br/> I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">doubt</span> that she found me interesting.<br/><br/><br/> My <span class=\\\"strong\\\">limbs</span> became <span class=\\\"strong\\\">numb</span>.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Linking and Deletion with Must  ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " When a word ending in consonant +/t/ links into a word beginning with a consonant, the final /t/ of the first word is often deleted. This is often the case with the word must.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you delete (or drop) the final /t/, the sound before the /t/ must link smoothly into the following word.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "  When the word <span class=\"italic\">have</span> follows <span class=\"italic\">must</span>,  <span class=\"italic\">have</span> is reduced to \"_ov\" or \"_av\".<br/> The 't' sound joins the reduced <span class=\"italic\">have</span>. <br/><br/>must have   =  mus_tuv or mus_tav ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Phrase\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Pronunciation\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" must find\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" mus_find\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" must be\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" mus_be\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" must have thought\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"mus_tuv thought<br/>mus_ta thought\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "You must be happy to have met a girl who likes the same things as you!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "She must have thought I was just a boring guy.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "She must have felt like I was just a waste of her time.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "dumb", "type": "name"}, {"content": " stupid; foolish", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I was so nervous that I kept saying dumb things all evening.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le11ob04aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about a first date.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to climb", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to go up an incline or staircase; to ascend", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I had to climb the stairs all the way to the top.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le11ob04aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "numb", "type": "name"}, {"content": " deprived of sensation and feeling", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My arms and legs felt numb.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le11ob04aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to doubt", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to feel uncertain about something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I doubt that she found me interesting.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le11ob04aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "limb", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an arm or leg", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I was so nervous that my limbs became numb.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le11ob04aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to comb", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to arrange hair by drawing a comb through it", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My hair was a mess and I didn't have time to comb it.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le11ob04aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Write a short story (12-14 lines) about a first date.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Think of a 